Relational analysis
centers — Avalokiteśvara as multi-layer anchor [scope: shrine]
Avalokiteśvara does not merely centre a single pair but anchors two concentric lateral systems simultaneously:
inner (guardians)
outer (bodhisattvas)
This creates a layered rather than flat lateral structure.

mirrors — dual mirroring system [scope: altar + shrine]
Two distinct mirroring relations operate:
Guan Yu ↔ Skanda → protective symmetry
Samantabhadra ↔ Mañjuśrī → doctrinal symmetry (practice–wisdom)
This produces functional mirroring at two different conceptual registers.

flanks — differentiated lateral hierarchy
Although all four figures flank the centre, they do so at different layers:
inner flanks → protection
outer flanks → doctrinal/cosmological framing
Flanking is therefore not uniform but stratified.

guards — inner protective ring
Only Guan Yu and Skanda participate in the guards relation. This distinguishes them sharply from the outer bodhisattvas, whose role is not defensive

